      "content": "i get that, but if u were designing the algorithm to be \"realistic\" based on real world data, wouldn't u have to account for the fact that people in places like riverside commons statistically face more systemic issues? like, aren't those neighborhoods often associated with lower socioeconomic stability or different demographic patterns that actually affect repayment rates in the real world? wouldnt its more \"accurate\" to bake those neighborhood demographics into the risk profile?",
